WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.789
Internet in many schools is weak or expensive. You can still teach digitally.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.903
Download once, then share offline by flash drive, memory card or Bluetooth.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:17.967
Choose light formats: text, PDF and audio use far less data than video.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.423
Use WhatsApp groups, SMS reminders, and printouts for learners without phones.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.432
And use save offline in Nexus, to open lessons without internet.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:40.507
Before you move on, check: Download one resource and share it offline. Choose text or audio instead of video. Save a lesson offline in Nexus. Submit your lesson plan.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:46.241
Well done. You have finished the course. Now plan a digital-literacy lesson.
